Task 6.4 (receipt email wording and its delivery row; F12 answered, D054 items 1 and 2; D023; D028; D032).
NOT LITERAL-ONLY since the 6.4 review (blocking finding 1): one created_at branch and two imports, below. Everything
else is inside a string or template literal.

1. The delivery row (D054 item 1, D023; legal-requirements ECOM-07). The receipt is sent once, at payment
   (src/lib/store/fulfil.ts notifyPaid, behind markPaid), so after launch every receipt belongs to a new order, and
   D023 allows "20 October 2026" in it only until the new site launches. The row now follows the /thanks order card
   by the ROW's created_at, with the card's own rule:
   - imports `deliveryLine` from src/lib/offer/delivery-line.ts (pure; never throws, so notifyPaid's never-throw rule
     holds; the same function the /thanks card's OrderRows section uses) and `DELIVERY_TEXT` from
     src/content/en-IN/delivery.ts (the one D023 value);
   - `AckInput.order` also picks "created_at". The one caller, frozen fulfil.ts, already passes the whole PreorderRow,
     so it is unchanged; created_at is `not null` in the schema;
   - before 10 October 2026, 00:00 IST: "Ships from" + SHIP_DATE_TEXT, byte-identical to the tag's row; on or after,
     and for a missing or unreadable date (P8): "Delivery" + DELIVERY_TEXT ("Deliveries start mid-November"), the
     /thanks card's labels (src/content/en-IN/store/confirmation.ts order.delivery).
   The frozen templates.test.ts is unchanged by this: its fixture was created 2026-08-22, before the cutoff, so it
   still pins SHIP_DATE_TEXT. The later orders are tested in test/email-delivery-line.test.ts (the frozen folder cannot
   gain a file), which also proves the receipt prints the same row as the /thanks card for the same order.
   RULED by the main session at the batch 6b merge (2026-10-14): accepted, because D054 item 1 and D023 need it; the
   rule moved from sections/store/OrderRows to src/lib/offer/delivery-line.ts so lib/email imports no section
   (structure §6); DELIVERY_TEXT comes in as src/lib/offer/offer.ts already takes it.
2. D028 (wiki/site/pages/store-confirmation.md fold 2): the balance row's label "Due on dispatch" becomes
   "Due before delivery" in the HTML row and in both plain-text branches (token and full payment), matching the
   /thanks order card (order.due.term). The token branch's sentence ends "of the <LAUNCH_PRICE> price (incl. GST)",
   as the /thanks row does (order.due.balance; D024: every price says "incl. GST").
3. D032: the support number takes calls as well as messages. The HTML footer's "The WhatsApp number takes messages,
   not calls." comes off and its lead reads "WhatsApp or call <number>, or write to <email>."; the plain text's
   "(messages, not calls)" comes off the same way. The link stays wa.me and the number and email stay
   SUPPORT_WHATSAPP_DISPLAY and CONTACT_EMAIL. (D032: calls must be answered before this goes live, Gate B.)
4. D028 (wiki/site/pages/store-confirmation.md, 'labels are copy for the build, to match this page'): the order
   reference's label "Order" becomes "Order number" in the HTML row and the plain text, as on the /thanks order card
   (confirmation.order.number); test/email-delivery-line.test.ts holds the two together. The internal alert's
   "Order" row is internal and stays.
Unchanged: amounts and the balance derived from the row, the tier and address branches, the refund promise, the
balance link on WhatsApp and by email, the seller block, the internal alert, the signature of preorderAckEmail.

